{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "10", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "03", "M": "41", "S": "21"}}, "news": [{"title": "Haryana RERA orders Pareena Infrastructure to pay compensation to buyers for  delay in flat handover", "para": "The Haryana Real Estate Regulatory Authority mandated Pareena Infrastructure to pay nearly Rs 23 lakh in compensation to two distressed homebuyers. This ruling followed significant delays in delivering their flats, triggering claims for financial strain and emotional distress. The developer is required to settle the amount within thirty days, covering both the buyers' loss of appreciation and litigation expenses.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/rera/haryana-rera-orders-pareena-infrastructure-to-pay-compensation-to-buyers-for-delay-in-flat-handover/133079796?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-49856/133079796.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "rera"}, {"title": "Pune town planning schemes\u2019 future in the dark as state cancels plans", "para": "Pune's town planning schemes face a bleak outlook as the state government has paused their progression. Some of these projects were already in the land acquisition phase, and the recent transition of two schemes in Uruli-Phursungi to a different municipal council only adds to the uncertainty. Urban development experts argue that this move could hinder the city's urgent urbanisation goals, even as other plans await action from PMRDA.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/pune-town-planning-schemes-future-in-the-dark-as-state-cancels-plans/133063374?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-39104/133063374.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Freehold relief in sight for Chandigarh\u2019s leasehold properties", "para": "The Ministry of Home Affairs is currently reviewing a proposal to convert leasehold properties to freehold status. This pivotal development emerges after extensive discussions among political figures and ministers. The Chandigarh administration, having secured the needed approvals, forwarded this proposal. It is anticipated that this change will enhance property values and stimulate investment within the city, along with providing updates on other property-related matters.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/freehold-relief-in-sight-for-chandigarhs-leasehold-properties/133063350?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-272616/133063350.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}